commit 3c0271cde7c97cb7e93308af218606f6fab7b7b0
Author: zetao.zhang <zetao.zhang@sophgo.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 17 08:21:36 2026 +0800

    feat(mobile): issue table column resize + reorder, row-level new sub-issue (MYS-1161)
    
    Web gets column resizing from TanStack Table's column sizing and column
    ordering from dnd-kit; the phone has neither, and its header has no hover.
    
    - Column widths: `tableColumnWidths` on the view store's table-columns slice
      (sparse overrides, clamped 64..360, cleared when set back to the default),
      driven by a PanResponder resize handle on each header's trailing edge. The
      drag keeps its provisional width locally and commits once on release; the
      header and the body lay out from one shared width array so the two synced
      panes cannot drift mid-drag. Data rows are memoised with an element-wise
      width comparison so a drag re-renders the header, not every row.
    - Column order: `reorderTableColumn` + per-column move rows in the column
      menu (a horizontal drag-to-reorder would fight the header scroller for the
      axis). `title` stays pinned first — a forward step is refused as well as a
      backward one, or the pinned column would swap into the scroller.
    - The column menu also shows the current display order and a reset.
    - Row-level "new sub-issue": the `+` web reveals on title hover is a
      permanent target on the phone's pinned title cell, hidden while selecting.
      It opens the new-issue form with the parent preset as route params (the
      same call web's `createSubIssue` makes), which the form shows as a
      removable chip and writes as `parent_issue_id`; the parent's project rides
      along.
    
    2385 tests green (baseline 2360).
    
    Co-authored-by: multica-agent <github@multica.ai>

